codex
The full-covariance variant is patched. I’m sweeping its off-diagonal scale; a good value would improve the analytic targets used by the MC corrections, but too large can amplify the nonzero-mean approximation error. 

exec
/bin/bash -lc "python - <<'PY'
import os
import re
import subprocess

values = [0.0, 0.05, 0.12, 0.25, 0.50, 0.85, 1.20]
for v in values:
    env = os.environ.copy()
    env['WB_FULL_COV_SCALE'] = str(v)
    proc = subprocess.run(['python', 'eval_client.py'], cwd='.', env=env, text=True, capture_output=True)
    out = proc.stdout + proc.stderr
    match = re.search(r'raw_score\\s+([0-9.eE+-]+)', out)
    score = match.group(1) if match else 'ERR'
    print(f'WB_FULL_COV_SCALE={v} raw_score={score}')
PY" in /opt/tiger/discover/workspace
